For teachers
Choose a question to try, then change the response to see which mathematical distinctions its grading preserves. The authoring guide explains how to bring your own questions to a page.

Algebraic equivalence and written form

Equivalent rational expression
The prompt states the domain \(x\ne -n\). A cancelled fraction and the original unreduced expression both receive full credit because the question asks for any equivalent expression on that domain. A reciprocal triggers a targeted feedback branch.
Variant Variant 1Variant 2Variant 3For \(x\neq-{4}\), give an expression equivalent to \(\dfrac{(x+{4})(x+{5})}{(x+{4})^2}\). You may simplify it, or give any equivalent expression on this domain.  Validate answersCheck answerRun question testsShow source```{.stack-question}
